ore  the ruins  [Music]  located in yemen is a palace that  appears to have been carved from the  rock that it sits on  however this man-made wonder was once  just a simple summer home  [Music]  just 10 miles away from yemen's capital  city of sanaa is da al hajjah otherwise  known as iman's rock palace  [Music]  in the early days of yemen's history the  country was led by the imam the islamic  spiritual leader rather than a king or  president  the rock palace was built in the 1930s  by imam yahar as his summer residence  however it is believed to have been  built over an older palace  the residence is five stories high has  several balconies and its own water  supply from a deep well  it is seen as an example of traditional  yemen architecture due to the patterned  windows earth tone coloring and  protruding exterior decorations  while tourism in this region is limited  due to conflict this palace is both a  sanctuary for locals and an example of  the man-made beauty of yemen  [Music]  located in postonia slovenia is a sturdy  castle built into a natural cavern  halfway up a 400-foot cliffside  [Music]  pradyama castle was built in the 13th  century in gothic-styled architecture  however after a siege in the 16th  century the exterior was reconstructed  and is what you see today  but there's more to this castle than  meets the eye  beneath it lays the postonia cave park  the caves are accessible during may to  september and closed in the winter so as  not to disturb the hibernating local  bats  the castle has changed ownership  throughout its history however the most  famous inhabitant was ezrim luga he was  a 15th century robin hood-like character  who stole from the rich to give to the  needy  today the castle and caves are open for  the public to explore and learn more  about its previous colorful owners  with more than 65 000 square feet of  space and 115 rooms hearst castle is one  of america's largest and most treasured  homes  hearst castle was built by american  newspaper magnate william randolphurst  in 1919 after he inherited 40 000 acres  of farmland  he would go on to purchase 200 000 more  acres of land allowing him to create the  kind of sprawling compound rarely seen  to this day  in addition to the main house la casa  grande hearst castle is comprised of  three guest houses an outdoor pool and  numerous other amenities  one of the most recognizable rooms in  the hearst castle is the 345 000 gallon  indoor roman pool  styled after ancient roman baths the  pool is decorated with eight statues of  roman and greek gods goddesses and  heroes  hearst was known for throwing lavish  parties and hosting important figures at  his san simeon home  winston churchill charlie chaplin cary  grant greta garbo and calvin coolidge  were some of the hundreds of house  guests  the home was donated to the state of  california in 1958 and welcomes more  than 750 000 visitors every year  [Music]  hidden away in the tuscan hills of  northern italy this beautiful moorish  castle was built in 1605  but for more than two decades it's been  sitting empty  there are 365 rooms in the castello di  samatsano  one for every day of the year  the moroccan style palatial villa is a  labyrinth of exquisitely tiled rooms  each one intricately unique  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  the castle was once a luxury hotel  restaurant and bar but closed its doors  in the early 1990s  it wasn't until 2013 that a local  non-profit committee was founded to help  raise awareness for the increasingly  decaying castle  they have no ownership of samatsano but  they helped to arrange and promote rare  public openings  [Music]  what you're seeing was built by one man  pebble by pebble  over 33 years  one morning mailman ferdinand chaval  stumbled across an interesting looking  stone on his delivery route  he picked it up  and from there an obsession began  using stones he collected on his walk  chaval worked each night without any  formal training to build what is now  called the palais ideal  the final structure is 85 feet long and  300 feet high  it mingles chinese algerian and northern  european influences to create a  fantastic and completely original castle  of grottoes  [Music]  he opened the palace in 1870 for the  public to enjoy  [Music]  in his own words he says  you start wondering if you have not been  carried away into a fantastic dream with  boundaries beyond the scope of  imagination  [Music]  and this incredible bizarre and unique  place  does look like something you could only  see in a dream  you

